        {
          "type": "points",
          "say": "But if A starts first, and B and C arrive ten seconds later, S J F is stuck again. Shortest time to completion first preempts: whenever a job arrives, it runs whichever job has the least time left. But turnaround isn't everything. Response time is the wait from arrival to first run, and it's what an interactive user feels. Round robin runs each job for a short time slice, in turn. Its response time is excellent, but its turnaround is close to the worst possible. And the slice length is a trade-off: shorter means snappier, but more context switches.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Turnaround or <em>response</em>?",
            "items": [
