          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Linux tracks a virtual runtime for every task: the CPU time it has used, scaled by its weight. Runnable tasks sit in a red black tree, ordered by virtual runtime, and the scheduler picks the leftmost: the task that has had the least. Task D runs, and its virtual runtime grows from 20 to 60. It's no longer the smallest, so it goes back into the tree, further right. Now B is the leftmost, and runs next. Over time, every task gets its fair share.",
